erent. Let me try listing incidents to see context, and maybe try other service names. The get_service_status returned \"Unknown service payments\" and list_deployments returned empty. Perhaps the service is named differently, e.g., \"payment\" or \"payments-service\". Let me check incidents for context.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a14135062e75d18a8f3934", "function": {"arguments": "{}", "name": "list_incidents"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service name \"payments\" returned an unknown service error. Let me try some likely variations to find the correct service name.", "reasoning_content": "The service \"payments\" is unknown. Let me think about what could be happening. Maybe the service name is different. Let me try some variations. The user said \"Payments\" service. Maybe it's \"payment\" or \"payment-service\" or \"payments-service\". Let me try a few.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413510487fc3b01f0095", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413510487fc3b01f00ad", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413510487fc3b01f00b6", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413510487fc3b01f00ce", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Let me try a few more likely service name variations.", "reasoning_content": "The service \"payments\" is unknown. Let me think about this. The user says \"Payments is throwing errors since this morning's deploy. Roll the affected payments service back to its most recent release that was healthy in production, and open a SEV2 incident for it.\"\n\nBut the tools say \"Unknown service payments\" and list_deployments returns empty. Maybe the service name is different. Let me try other names like \"billing\", \"checkout\", \"payments-api\", \"payment-gateway\", etc. But I don't have a way to list services. Let me try a few more variations.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a141354cfb7061b3fc64ef", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a141354cfb7061b3fc64f3", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-gateway\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a141354cfb7061b3fc6506", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"billing\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a141354cfb7061b3fc6510", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"checkout\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Found it \u2014 the service is `payments-api`, currently on v5.1.0, unhealthy with an 18% error rate. Let me check its deployment history to find the most recent healthy release.", "reasoning_content": "The service is `payments-api`. It's currently on v5.1.0, unhealthy with an 18% error rate. Let me check the deployment history to find the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413588287f52804f57f1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The deployment history confirms it: v5.1.0 (current) is degraded, and v5.0.0 was the last healthy release in production. I'll roll back to v5.0